<p align="left" class="body1"><span class="body1 style73"> <h2>News archive</h2><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-02-21 | Wednesday</font></strong><br/><br/><img alt="Archived image unavailable" height="360" width="160"><br><br>Look, i'm not playin. Us Massliners really <em>are</em> everywhere. Another case in point: Massline forum member/restauranteur/injera pusher <strong>Rawita</strong> aka <strong>Rahwa Habte</strong> (left) is featured in this week's <strong>Stranger</strong>, calling her (and her sister <strong>Asmeret</strong>) restaurant, <strong>Hidmo</strong>, a <em>hip hop mecca</em>. Peep out the article <a class="massline-external-gap" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20090315005801/http://thestranger.com/seattle/Content?oid=161460" rel="noopener noreferrer">here</a>, and come thru to Hidmo <a href="/bluescholars/massline-forums/topic-1148-page-0.html">this Friday night</a>, as <strong>Sabzi</strong> and myself will be spinning the cuts for y'all. You might need a band aid for all them cuts! Shout out to Charles Mudede for the article.<p></p><br/><hr align="center" noshade="" size="1" width="400"/><br/><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-02-21 | Wednesday</font></strong><br/><br/>Six degrees of Massline: There's no <strong>Kevin Bacon</strong> involved in this, but as some of you know, comedian <strong>Hari Kondabolu</strong> was on <em>Jimmy Kimmel Live!</em> last Monday night. You see, he's connected to Massline because he done did a Massline-sponsored comedy show in January (hosted by <strong>Sabzi</strong> and <strong>Khingz</strong>), wrote and starred in a film short directed by Sabzi's brother <strong>Zia</strong>, and brands his own comedy with responsible social commentary that is parallel to what Massline is all about.<br><br>The other connection this week comes from rival network NBC. Massline board member <strong>HAUNT</strong> - who did separate flyers for January's <strong>Common Market</strong> and <strong>Blue Scholars</strong> shows - appeared on <em>Conan O'Brien</em> last week with his girlfriend for a Valentine's Day sketch:<br><br><br><br><br><p class="massline-embed-gap">Archived embedded media is unavailable for offline playback. <a class="massline-external-playback" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4ynn_rHJhl0" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open video 4ynn_rHJhl0 on YouTube (external playback)</a></p><br><br><br>Watch out y'all, us Massliners are everywhere!<br>Peace<br>dj daps1<br> <p></p><br/><hr align="center" noshade="" size="1" width="400"/><br/><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-02-20 | Tuesday</font></strong><br/><br/>Bay Area / West Koast stand up!!! More dates for the <strong>Stop the Killings Tour</strong> to be announced in the near future.<br><br><img alt="Archived image unavailable" height="478" width="361"><br><br><img alt="Archived image unavailable" height="479" width="360"><br><br>It's also Tuesday, which means a short work/school week, which means we're gettin' closer to the <strong>Lovework CD Release Party</strong>! Info on the show listed on the right hand side. Here's the flyer if you've been living under a boulder (or if you're from <strong>Boulder</strong> and you have no idea what of what i'm talkin about):<br><br><img alt="Archived image unavailable" height="361" width="275"><br><br>We also would like to give a big shout out to our fellow funny dude and Massline supporter, comedian <a class="massline-external-gap" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20090315005801/http://youtube.com/results?search_query=hari+kondabolu&amp;search=Search" rel="noopener noreferrer">Hari Kondabolu</a>, who appeared on last night's <em>Jimmy Kimmel Live!</em> Congratulations!<br><br>peace<br>dj daps1<p></p><br/><hr align="center" noshade="" size="1" width="400"/><br/><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-02-19 | Monday</font></strong><br/><br/><img alt="Archived image unavailable" height="323" width="430"><br><br>HAPPY BORN DAY TO YOUR EMCEES FAVORITE EMCEE, GEOLOGIC! Give him a shout out <strong><a href="/bluescholars/massline-forums/topic-1143-page-0.html">here</a></strong><a href="/bluescholars/massline-forums/topic-1143-page-0.html">.</a><br><em><br/></em>Peace<br>dj daps1<em><br><br/>Photo taken by me in July of 2003 for the Wing Luke Asian Museum's hip hop exhibit.</br></em> <p></p><br/><hr align="center" noshade="" size="1" width="400"/><br/><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-02-19 | Monday</font></strong><br/><br/>happy monday all.<br><br>today is an important day, folkers.  because it's president's day? <br><br>HAHAHAHAHAHAHAHA.<br/><br/><br/>no.<br/><br/>actually, there's a few things goin on.  for those who had the fortunate opportunity of attending the <strong>MASSLINE Presents: Stand Up Comedy!</strong> show, you will remember our good friend <strong>Hari Kondabolu</strong>.  well, tonight <strong>Hari</strong> will be featuring on the late <strong>Jimmy Kimmel</strong> show.  so, if you're up that late, tune in and support our fellow Seattlite speak some truth on national television.<br/><br/>many ups that are "big" in nature go to our <strong>206 Zulu</strong> homies.  from the showcase that was at the Sundiata Festival to the extensive line up at Neumo's shortly after, the local Zulu chapter put in hella work this past weekend to see that hip hop was represented substantially.<br/><br/>the countdown to the release of <strong>Gabriel Teodros' "Lovework"</strong> is nearing its end.  i'll tell you that i'm pumped like a pair of mid-90's Reebok sneakers.<br/><br/>yessir.<br/><br/>saba<p></p><br/><hr align="center" noshade="" size="1" width="400"/><br/><center><div class="pagenumbers"><a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-f410280b6a12.php">[&lt;&lt;]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-ff41e4b899bf.php">[1]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-f09e4ab70de0.php">[2]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-13fd6b501db4.php">[3]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-a6d8d32ad781.php">[4]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-d45f54b0cbc4.php">[5]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-0bfc403792bc.php">[6]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-fd78b8847920.php">[7]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-cd30dd4ecbb4.php">[8]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-3f0473af164e.php">[9]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-328a9b624d92.php">[10]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-3c1fe8996261.php">[11]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-86e16e039033.php">[12]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-7e9b30d94f52.php">[13]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-a4c814fd9062.php">[14]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-9413aa1ebf0f.php">[15]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-c3d2d6995e50.php">[16]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-9d70a3c73aca.php">[17]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-f6fd84ec4403.php">[18]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-aeb25bb8527b.php">[19]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-b69d705746cb.php">[20]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-a5db3a75cdf8.php">[21]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-7369bee5daae.php">[22]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-1dbf17b25e1a.php">[23]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/news/archive-a2d6ccd834ab.php">[24]</a> <a href="/bluescholars/masslinemedia/site/n